    "### Chunk, embed, and retrieve\n",
    "Each document is chunked separately, therefore no chunk mixes text from two documents. `SOURCES` records which document each chunk came from.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Config | How it cuts | Chunks |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| small (120/20) | every 120 characters, 20 overlap (starter) | 5,631 |\n",
    "| large (320/40) | every 320 characters, 40 overlap (starter) | 2,013 |\n",
    "| by-sentence | whole sentences packed up to 500 characters | 1,209 |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why by-sentence replaces the starter's by-paragraph.** \n",
    "\n",
    "by-paragraph splits on blank lines, and PDF extraction produces almost none. On this corpus it produced only 22 chunks, averaging about 26,000 characters each. The embedding model reads at most 256 tokens (roughly 1,000 characters) and ignores the rest, so most of each chunk would have been invisible to search. Sentence endings survive PDF extraction, therefore by-sentence keeps the idea of cutting at natural boundaries whilst staying under the model's limit. `chunk_paragraph` is left in the cell as the record of that result.\n",
    "\n",
    "`build` and `retrieve` are unchanged from the starter."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "1d524b01",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "small (120/20)   -> 5631 chunks\n",
      "large (320/40)   -> 2013 chunks\n",
      "by-sentence      -> 1209 chunks\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def chunk_fixed(text, size, overlap):\n",
    "    text = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', text).strip(); out, i = [], 0\n",
    "    while i < len(text):\n",
    "        out.append(text[i:i+size]); i += size - overlap\n",
    "    return out\n",
    "def chunk_paragraph(text):\n",
    "    return [re.sub(r'\\s+',' ',p).strip() for p in text.split('\\n\\n') if p.strip()]\n",
    "\n",
    "def chunk_sentences(text, max_chars=500):\n",
    "    text = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', text).strip()\n",
    "    sentences = re.split(r'(?<=[.!?])\\s+', text)\n",
    "    chunks, current = [], ''\n",
    "    for s in sentences:\n",
    "        if current and len(current) + len(s) + 1 > max_chars:\n",
    "            chunks.append(current)\n",
    "            current = s\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            current = (current + ' ' + s).strip()\n",
    "    if current:\n",
    "        chunks.append(current)\n",
    "    return chunks\n",
    "\n",
    "def chunk_corpus(chunker):\n",
    "    chunks, sources = [], []\n",
    "    for name, text in CLEAN.items():\n",
    "        for c in chunker(text):\n",
    "            chunks.append(c)\n",
    "            sources.append(name)\n",
    "    return chunks, sources\n",
    "\n",
    "configs, SOURCES = {}, {}\n",
    "for label, chunker in {'small (120/20)': lambda t: chunk_fixed(t, 120, 20),\n",
    "                       'large (320/40)': lambda t: chunk_fixed(t, 320, 40),\n",
    "                       'by-sentence':   chunk_sentences}.items():\n",
    "    configs[label], SOURCES[label] = chunk_corpus(chunker)\n",
    "\n",
    "for n, c in configs.items():\n",
    "    print(f'{n:16s} -> {len(c)} chunks')\n",
    "\n",
    "def build(chunks):\n",
    "    e = embedder.encode(chunks, normalize_embeddings=True).astype('float32')\n",
    "    idx = faiss.IndexFlatIP(e.shape[1]); idx.add(e); return idx\n",
    "def retrieve(idx, chunks, q, k=3):\n",
    "    qe = embedder.encode([q], normalize_embeddings=True).astype('float32')\n",
    "    # FAISS uses -1 for missing results when fewer than k chunks exist.\n",
    "    return [chunks[i] for i in idx.search(qe, k)[1][0] if i >= 0]"
   ]
  },
