    "### Chunk-level precision and recall (k = 3)\n",
    "- **Precision@3** = relevant chunks retrieved / 3. Of what would be handed to the LLM, how much is useful?\n",
    "- **Recall@3** = relevant chunks retrieved / all relevant chunks in that config. Of everything that could have been found, how much was?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Questions with no relevant chunk.** \n",
    "\n",
    "A fixed-size chunker can cut a fact in half at a chunk boundary. If that happens everywhere the fact appears, no chunk contains the whole fact, recall cannot be calculated (it would divide by zero), and the question is counted here instead. The result was zero for all three configs: every fact survived whole in at least one chunk."
   ]
